---
import Page from '../../layouts/Page.astro';
import { breadcrumbs } from '../../components/_breadcrumbs';
import { downloads } from '../../config/downloads';

const comparisons = [
  {
    href: '/compare/niyora-vs-flo/',
    them: 'Flo',
    line: 'A full cycle tracker that logs and predicts, then stops. Niyora predicts your window too, then helps you through the hard hour.',
  },
  {
    href: '/compare/niyora-vs-clue/',
    them: 'Clue',
    line: 'A precise cycle and symptom tracker built on data. Niyora is the thing you open when a feeling actually lands.',
  },
  {
    href: '/compare/niyora-vs-ai-companion/',
    them: 'an AI companion',
    line: 'A general chatbot that will talk about anything. Niyora is built for one window, the days before your period.',
  },
  {
    href: '/compare/privacy/',
    them: 'every cycle app on data',
    line: 'What nine cycle apps told Apple and wrote in their own privacy policies, side by side, with a link to every source.',
  },
  {
    href: '/compare/moon-ai-vs-other-ai/',
    them: 'other AI',
    line: 'Most AI keeps you talking and learns from what you type. Moon is built for the hard moment and knows almost nothing about you.',
  },
];

const crumbs = breadcrumbs([{ name: 'Compare', href: '/compare/' }, { name: 'Alternatives to mood trackers', href: '/compare/alternatives-to-mood-trackers/' }]);
---

<Page
  title="Alternatives to mood trackers that do more than log · Niyora"
  description="Tired of trackers that only log and predict? Niyora predicts your PMS window too, then helps you through it: reflect, regulate, respond. No account."
  canonicalUrl="https://niyora.com/compare/alternatives-to-mood-trackers/"
  jsonLd={crumbs}
>
  <section class="s hero">
    <div class="eyebrow">Alternatives to mood trackers</div>
    <h1>Tired of tracking your mood and getting only a chart? There is more.</h1>
    <p class="lead">Most mood and period apps do the same thing: they log, they predict, they show you a chart, and there they stop. Niyora tracks and predicts your PMS window too, but it does not stop at the chart. It helps you through the moment a hard premenstrual feeling actually lands, and its training builds the skill before you need it.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="s">
    <div class="moat">
      <p>A tracker tells you it is coming, then leaves you to handle it. Niyora predicts the same window, then <strong>shows up when it lands</strong>: reflect, regulate, respond in about a minute, and training that builds the skill before you need it. The prediction is where a tracker finishes. For Niyora it is where the help starts.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="s">
    <h2>Why people look for an alternative</h2>
    <ul class="why-list">
      <li>The prediction lands, but nothing shows up to help you in the window it points to.</li>
      <li>A chart of what you felt last month does not help you in the moment you feel it now.</li>
      <li>Your most private feelings are sitting in an account, tied to your cycle, forever.</li>
      <li>You do not just want more data about yourself. You want to feel steadier, faster.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="s">
    <h2>Niyora compared, side by side</h2>
    <p class="lead">Honest comparisons, no trash talk. Many people will use a tracker and Niyora both. Niyora tracks too, so the difference is what it does with the prediction.</p>
    <div class="picks">
      {comparisons.map((c) => (
        <a class="pick" href={c.href}>
          <div class="pick-head">Niyora vs {c.them}</div>
          <p>{c.line}</p>
          <span class="pick-go">Read the comparison →</span>
        </a>
      ))}
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="s">
    <h2>Not sure the hard week is even PMS?</h2>
    <p class="lead">Take the two-minute check and see how your premenstrual week actually hits.</p>
    <div class="cta-row">
      <a href="/quiz" class="btn">Take the quiz</a>
      <a href={downloads.appStore} class="btn ghost">Get Niyora</a>
    </div>
  </section>
</Page>

<style>
  /* Page-specific only: the moat callout, the reasons list, and the pick
     cards. Shared chrome (sheet, sections, dividers, type scale, buttons,
     footer) comes from Page's global CSS. */
  .moat {
    max-width: 720px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 32px 30px;
    border-radius: 20px;
    border: 1px solid rgba(var(--accent-rgb), 0.28);
    background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.03);
  }
  .moat p { font-size: 21px; font-weight: 300; line-height: 1.5; color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.86); max-width: none; margin: 0; }
  .moat strong { color: rgba(var(--accent-rgb), 0.98); font-weight: 500; }

  .why-list {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin: 8px auto 0;
    max-width: 640px;
    text-align: left;
    display: grid;
    gap: 14px;
  }
  .why-list li {
    padding: 16px 20px;
    border-radius: 14px;
    border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08);
    background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.03);
    font-size: 16px;
    font-weight: 300;
    line-height: 1.55;
    color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.78);
  }

  .picks {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(240px, 1fr));
    gap: 16px;
    width: 100%;
    max-width: 900px;
    margin: 24px auto 0;
    text-align: left;
  }
  .pick {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 10px;
    padding: 24px 24px 22px;
    border-radius: 18px;
    border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08);
    background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.03);
    text-decoration: none;
    transition: transform 0.3s ease, border-color 0.3s ease;
  }
  .pick:hover { transform: translateY(-3px); border-color: rgba(var(--accent-rgb), 0.45); }
  .pick-head { font-size: 18px; font-weight: 500; color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.94); }
  .pick p { font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.55; color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.66); margin: 0; max-width: none; }
  .pick-go { font-size: 14px; color: rgba(var(--accent-rgb), 0.9); }

  .cta-row { display: flex; gap: 16px; flex-wrap: wrap; justify-content: center; margin-top: 28px; }

  @media (max-width: 720px) {
    .s { padding: 56px 24px; }
    h1 { font-size: 34px; }
    h2 { font-size: 26px; }
    .moat p { font-size: 18px; }
  }
</style>
